dHouse

Tasmota manager for Sonoff devices
dHouse is an open-source application for managing Sonoff devices running the Tasmota firmware. 
It is strongly inspired by the eWeLink software.
dHouse requires a Linux server to operate. 
It uses the MQTT protocol to communicate to Tasmota devices.

Required third-party software: 
	Avahi – for local network service discovery 
	Mosquitto – as the MQTT broker 
	SortableJS – for drag-and-drop UI functionality 
	Ntfy – for push notifications
	SQLite3 - for data logging

dHouse runs through a web interface built with PHP and JavaScript. 


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Installation
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

dHouse is designed to run on a Debian-based Linux server.
Apache home for this document is /usr/local/dhouse/web
Copy the whole master/src files to /usr/local/dhouse

Set MQTT_SERVER value in config.php file.
[/usr/local/dhouse/web/config.php]

define("MQTT_SERVER", "xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx");	// place your mqtt server address

Apache:
	-Install Apache, php and php-curl.

	> apt install apache2 apache2-utils php php-curl

	-Set Apache permissions:
	[/etc/apache2/sites-available/000-default.conf]

	DocumentRoot /usr/local/dhouse/web
	<Directory /usr/local/dhouse/web>
	    AllowOverride AuthConfig
	</Directory>

	-Create .htaccess file in home folder:
	[/usr/local/dhouse/web/.htaccess]:

	AuthType Basic
	AuthName "dHouse Access"
	AuthUserFile /etc/apache2/dhouse.passwd
	Require valid-user	

	-Create password file:

	> htpasswd -c /etc/apache2/dhouse.passwd username
	
Avahi:

	> apt install avahi avahi-utils

Mosquitto:

	> apt install mosquitto

	-Set mosquito configuration into file /etc/mosquitto/conf.d:
	[auth.conf]

	per_listener_settings true
	listener 1883
	allow_anonymous true
	protocol mqtt

	-Restart mosquitto:

	> systemctl restart mosquitto


SQLite3:

	> apt install sqlite3 php-sqlite3

	-Run the script "create_tables.sql" from the folder db
	-Set dhouse.db database file to owner www-data

	> chown www-data:www-data dhouse.db


ntfy:
	-Notify is required to send notifications to cellphone.

	* IMPORTANT *

	The Ntfy service will be exposed to the Internet on port 8082.
	Make sure to set a strong, non-trivial username and password for this server.

	-Install ntfy from github repository:

	> wget https://github.com/binwiederhier/ntfy/releases/download/v2.12.0/ntfy_2.12.0_linux_amd64.deb
	> sudo dpkg -i ntfy_2.12.0_linux_amd64.deb
	> sudo systemctl enable ntfy
	> sudo systemctl start ntfy

	-Create user and password access for ntfy:

	> ntfy user add [username] --auth-file /etc/ntfy/user.db
	> ntfy user change-pass [username]

	-Edit file /etc/ntfy/server.yml and add following lines:
	[/etc/ntfy/server.yml]

	listen-http: ":8082"
	base-url: "http://dhouse.ddns.net:8082"
	auth-file: "/etc/ntfy/user.db"
	allow-unauthenticated: []
	web-root: disable

	-Install ntfy Application in your cellphone
	-Send a test message:

	> curl -u [username]:[password] -d "Testing!" http://[your ip address]:8082/dhouse

	-Set dhouse/ntfy .htaccess file:
	[/usr/local/dhouse/ntfy/.htaccess]

	Require all denied /

	-Create ntfy.json file into ntfy folder
	This is the file that dhouse_service will read for send notifications.

	[/usr/local/dhouse/ntfy/ntfy.json]

	{
  	"user": "username",
  	"password": "password",
  	"url": "http://[your ip address]:8082/dhouse"
	}

	
Apache proxy configuration	

dHouse uses a proxy to accelerate connections to and from the MQTT broker.
The proxy listens in 8080 port and uses Apache redirection for security.
Install next modules:

	> a2enmod proxy
	> a2enmod proxy_http
	> a2enmod proxy_wstunnel

Edit the Apache virtual host and add next lines:

	<virtualhost [your virtual host]>
      ProxyPass "/ws/" "ws://localhost:8080/ws/"
      ProxyPassReverse "/ws/" "ws://localhost:8080/ws/"

      <Directory /usr/local/dhouse>
         AllowOverride AuthConfig
      </Directory>

This works the same way for https, Apache makes connection from https to http for ws.


Services:

dHouse uses two services: proxy and dhouse itself.
Copy the file dhouse.service from "services" folder to /etc/systemd/system.
Copy the file dhouse_proxy.service from "proxy" folder to /etc/systemd/system.
Modify dhouse_proxy.py for the required MQTT_HOST and MQTT_PORT.

MQTT_HOST = "localhost"
MQTT_PORT = 1883

-Start services:

> systemctl daemon-reload
> systemctl start dhouse
> systemctl start dhouse_proxy


Open your browser get connected to the dHouse page.
Open Settings and place site name for initial configuration.


Enjoy!



